  "feedback": "# Message to Agent 1: New Curve Generation Instructions\n\n## Analysis of Top 3 Performing Curves\n\nThe top 3 curves have converged on an optimal design pattern with exceptional scores (0.942, 0.940, 0.940):\n\n**Key Success Factors:**\n\n1. **High Line Density**: All three use `num_lines = 300`, which is critical for achieving uniform sample density scores of 0.99+\n\n2. **Multi-Frequency Perturbation Strategy**: The winning curves employ 4-5 independent sinusoidal perturbations with:\n   - **Prime number frequencies** (13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37, 41) - this prevents harmonic resonance and creates more uniform space-filling\n   - **Small amplitudes**: x perturbations: 0.008-0.012, y perturbations: 0.003-0.008\n   - **Dual-axis approach**: Separate perturbations on both x and y axes rather than single-axis\n\n3. **Frequency Ranges**: \n   - X-axis primary: 17-19 (with amplitudes 0.008-0.009)\n   - X-axis secondary: 31-37 (with amplitudes 0.003-0.004)\n   - Y-axis primary: 22-23 (with amplitudes 0.007-0.008)\n   - Y-axis secondary: 29-41 (with amplitudes 0.003)\n\n4. **Coupled Perturbations**: curve_5_v7.py introduced a coupled term `coupled_amp * sin(2\u03c0 * coupled_freq * (x + y))` with amplitude 0.004 and frequency 13, which achieved the highest score.\n\n## Instructions: Generate 5 New Variations\n\nCreate exactly **5 new curves** exploring these specific modifications:\n\n**Variation 1: Enhanced Coupling**\n- Base: curve_5_v7.py structure\n- Add a second coupled term: `coupled_amp_2 = 0.003`, `coupled_freq_2 = 11` (another prime)\n- Use both `sin(2\u03c0 * 13 * (x+y))` and `sin(2\u03c0 * 11 * (x-y))` \n- Keep all other parameters identical to curve_5_v7.py\n\n**Variation 2: Extended Frequency Spectrum**\n- Base: curve_2_v7.py structure  \n- Add a third perturbation layer on each axis\n- X-axis tertiary: amplitude 0.002, frequency 43\n- Y-axis tertiary: amplitude 0.002, frequency 47\n- Keep primary/secondary parameters from curve_2_v7.py\n\n**Variation 3: Amplitude Optimization**\n- Base: curve_5_v7.py structure\n- Reduce x_amp_1 to 0.007 (from 0.008)\n- Increase y_amp_1 to 0.008 (from 0.007)\n- Increase coupled_amp to 0.005 (from 0.004)\n- Keep all frequencies unchanged\n\n**Variation 4: Higher Line Density**\n- Base: curve_2_v5.py structure\n- Increase `num_lines = 350` (from 300)\n- Proportionally reduce perturbation amplitudes by 15%:\n  - perturbation_amplitude_x = 0.0102 (from 0.012)\n  - perturbation_amplitude_y = 0.0068 (from 0.008)\n- Keep frequencies at 18 and 22\n\n**Variation 5: Hybrid Best Features**\n- Combine the best elements: 300 lines + 6 total perturbations + coupling\n- X: amp=[0.008, 0.003, 0.002], freq=[17, 31, 43]\n- Y: amp=[0.007, 0.003, 0.002], freq=[23, 29, 47]  \n- Coupled: amp=0.004, freq=13 on (x+y)\n- Use the curve_5_v7.py code structure as template\n\n**Critical Requirements:**\n- Maintain N=1000, serpent"
